@goun7 @atmpushout-jpg One scoping note and one offer for the negative-vector set, from the response-provenance side.

**Scope first.** GVP does not cover settled-not-delivered, delivered-not-settled, or payee mismatch, and I would not claim it does. It is a canonical SHA-256 over `{endpoint, inputs, result, method, dataVintage}`: it commits to what the answer said, and says nothing about whether money moved or who was paid. Those three vectors belong to the settlement and delivery planes @giskard09 describes. GVP is an input below them, at most.

**The offer is the method, not the vectors.**

